# The Met Museum
Artworks of the Metropolitan Museum of Art, found by what you type.
Every thing it shows is in MetMuseum.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  the type below adds to its type there,
with `<spell-more-of>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
Its search answers only ids:  each artwork is read from its own address as it's drawn, a page at a time, and no others.

<spell-thing "met museum page">
	<spell>
		- its "search" is text
		- to create it:
			set its search to "sunflowers"
	</spell>
	<property "found" description="What the Met finds for the search, looking at all of each artwork:  ids only, each read as it's drawn">every artwork matching the search</property>

	<action "try (words as text)">
		set its search to words
	</action>

	<draw>
		<form value={it} class="find">
			<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="center" justify="between">
				<header size="large">Artworks, from the Met</header>
				<ui-search name="search" parameter="art" icon="search" placeholder="A title, an artist, a subject" aria-label="Search the Met" />
			</stack>
			<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="center" spacing="xs">
				<text size="small" color="grey">Try</text>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "sunflowers"}>Sunflowers</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "van gogh"}>Van Gogh</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "armor"}>Armor</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "egypt"}>Egypt</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "cats"}>Cats</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "hokusai"}>Hokusai</button>
			</stack>
		</form>
		<for its found as="cards" layout="mosaic" columns="4" doubling paging="pages" loading="Asking the Met" failed="The Met can't be reached just now." empty="The Met has nothing for that." />
		<text class="credits" size="small" paragraph>
			From <link link="https://metmuseum.github.io">the Met Museum's API</link>, each artwork asked for as it's shown.  Press a picture to turn it over.
		</text>
	</draw>
</spell-thing>


# An artwork
A card that turns over:  its picture on the front, what the Met knows of it on the back.
Each is read from its own address the first time it's drawn;  one the Met won't give is left out.
Only what's in the public domain has a picture:  the rest show their title alone.

<spell-more-of "artwork">
	<draw>
		<if its title>
			<shape class="artwork" direction="over" flip-on="click" aria-label={its title}>
				<side>
					<ui-card fluid>
						<if its primary image small>
							<image src={its primary image small} alt={its title} />
						</if>
						<content>
							<header>{its title}</header>
							<meta>{its artist display name}</meta>
						</content>
					</ui-card>
				</side>
				<side>
					<ui-card fluid>
						<content>
							<header>{its title}</header>
							<meta>{its artist display name} · {its object date}</meta>
							<description>
								<text paragraph>{its medium}</text>
								<text paragraph>{its dimensions}</text>
								<text paragraph color="grey">{its department} · {its credit line}</text>
							</description>
						</content>
						<extra>
							<link link={its object url} target="_blank">On the Met's own pages</link>
						</extra>
					</ui-card>
				</side>
			</shape>
		</if>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>
